(6819,'Export a single configuration item to a file. See @config_overview_topic for more information about configuration.','','11.1.9'),
(6820,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>Configuration synchronization</em> &gt; <em>Export</em> &gt; <em>@single_export_link</em>.','','11.1.9'),
(6821,'Select the <em>Configuration type</em> that you want to export, and then select the specific <em>Configuration name</em> to export.','','11.1.9'),
(6822,'Use your browser to copy the text in the box marked <em>Here is your configuration</em> to the clipboard.','','11.1.9'),
(6823,'Paste the copied text into a plain-text editor on your computer or other device, and save it using the suggested file name below the text box.','','11.1.9'),
(6824,'Importing your complete site configuration','','11.1.9'),
(6825,'Import the complete configuration of your site from an archive file, such as one that was previously exported (see @export_full_topic). See @config_overview_topic for more information about configuration.','','11.1.9'),
(6826,'In the <em>Manage</em> administrative menu, navigate to <em>Configuration</em> &gt; <em>Development</em> &gt; <em>Configuration synchronization</em> &gt; <em>@import_link</em>.','','11.1.9'),
(6827,'Browse to find the <em>Configuration archive</em> that you want to import.','','11.1.9'),
